    s_SOMEONE_REPLY(py_dict(vec![(py_str("known"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("Since there is already a diagnosis, make this change the GP's problem rather than yours to watch: a step down like that is often something treatable, and an infection is the usual one they check for first."), py_str("Ring the GP about your {who} rather than waiting for the next appointment — a change that comes on over days rather than months is often something with a fix, and worth saying today.")])), (py_str("homeward"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("That's a relief — home is where most of the getting better happens. How is your {who} in themselves?"), py_str("Good news. Keep the first week small: short visits, early nights, and let your {who} set the pace rather than the other way round."), py_str("Home, then — that is the bit that matters. The first days back are the ones to keep quiet, because everyone tries to do too much in them."), py_str("Glad to hear it, and home beats a ward for getting better. Ask what to watch for in your {who}'s first fortnight, and who to ring if something changes.")])), (py_str("diagnosed"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("I'm sorry - a diagnosis like that changes the shape of a week. How is your {who} in themselves?"), py_str("Worrying news. What have they said about what happens next, and who is looking after your {who}'s care?"), py_str("That is a lot to take in, and it takes time to sink in. Has anyone walked you through the treatment yet?")])), (py_str("hospital"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("Sorry to hear that. How is your {who} doing?"), py_str("That is a worrying place for your {who} to be. What has the hospital said?"), py_str("Worrying, and waiting is the worst part of it. How is your {who} in themselves?")])), (py_str("memory"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("Losing track of things in a familiar place is worth a word with your {who}'s GP, and soon: it can be a lot of things and several of them are fixable. A note of when it started, and anything else that has changed, is what they ask for first."), py_str("That is worth mentioning to a GP rather than waiting to see if it settles. Write down what you have noticed about your {who} and when it started, and take that with you — and if it gets suddenly worse, that is the same day rather than next week."), py_str("Worth a GP appointment with your {who}, and take this line with you: forgetting things in a place they know well is the kind of change that gets looked at properly, and the sooner the easier it usually is.")])), (py_str("falls"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("A fall is worth getting looked at even when nothing hurts, and a second one is worth a GP visit: balance, eyesight and medicines are the usual causes and all three can be helped. Clear the loose rugs and put a lamp within reach of the bed in the meantime."), py_str("Falls are rarely just age, and that is the good news: strength, eyesight and medication are the places to look, and a GP can start on all three. Until then, good light on the stairs and nothing to trip over on the way to the bathroom.")])), (py_str("care"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("Ask the staff what they notice day to day and get it written in the home's notes — they see more of your {who} than you can, and a GP takes their record seriously. Visit at different times of day so you see it for yourself too."), py_str("A home keeps a daily record, so ask what is in it about your {who}: eating, sleep, and anything that has changed. That is the account a GP or the manager can act on, and it costs you one conversation at the desk.")])), (py_str("sleep"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("Broken sleep is worth reading rather than enduring: pain, a new tablet, drinking later, a room that is too warm, worry — one of those is usually behind it, and the fix is different for each. If it has been weeks, or they are worn out all day, ring the GP: a blood test rules out the physical ones."), py_str("A night that is nothing like their usual is a change worth having looked at, and sooner if it came on suddenly. Ring the GP this week and say when it started and what is different about the nights now.")])), (py_str("low"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("Going quiet and off things is worth saying out loud to a GP — it is common, it is treatable, and people often do not mention it themselves. One small thing a week that gets your {who} out, even a short walk, does more than a big plan."), py_str("That kind of withdrawal is worth a GP appointment rather than a wait: low mood in later life is under-reported and it responds to help. In the meantime, keep the visits going even when they say no — company is the bit that works.")])), (py_str("ill"), py_tuple(vec![py_str("Get your {who} looked at rather than waiting it out, and sooner if it is getting worse — a change like that in someone you are looking after is worth a proper check."), py_str("Worth a GP appointment for your {who} this week rather than next month, and keep a note of what has changed and when. If it turns sudden, that is the same day.")]))]));
